=== Suesha ===
* Toshogu Shrine - Enshrined deity: {{ill|lt=Tokugawa Ieyasu|Q171977|WD=Q171977|lt=Tokugawa Ieyasu|1=Tokugawa Ieyasu}}<ref name=":0">{{Cite web|Japanese book|url=https://niukawakami-jinja.jp/keidai/#keidai_16|title=Summer shrines, Toshogu Shrine and Mizu Shrine/Guide to the precincts|accessdate=2021.11.8|publisher=Niukawakami Shrine}}</ref>.
*Water Shrine - Deities enshrined: Takani no kami (enshrined deity at the upper shrine of Nyukawakami Shrine), Yami no kami (enshrined deity at the lower shrine of Nyu Kawakami Shrine)<ref name=":0" />.
*Kodama Shrine - Enshrined deity: {{ill|UNKNOWN|lt=Goju no Mikoto|1=UNKNOWN}}. 1982 ({{ill|lt=Showa|Q327567|WD=Q327567|1=Shōwa era}}57) To commemorate the 30th anniversary of the opening of the Ogawa-go Timber and Forest Products Cooperative Market, the shrine was founded at the request of {{ill|lt=Itaigeso Shrine|Q11379271|WD=Q11379271|1=Itakiso shrine}} (Wakayama City, Wakayama Prefecture)<ref>{{Cite web|Japanese book|url=https://niukawakami-jinja.jp/keidai/#keidai_18|title=Suesha/Koda Shrine/Guide to the precincts|accessdate=2021.11.8|publisher=Niukawakami Shrine}}</ref>.
